    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d454">

                <pb facs="0837" n="823" xml:id="pg823"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish, Secretary of
                        State, to Mr. Robeson, Secretary of the
                        Navy.</hi>
                </head>
                <dateline><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1869-11-11"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi>
                        11, 1869</date>.</dateline>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith a
                    transcript of a communication from the United States marshal for the southern
                    district of New York, of yesterday’s date, and will thank you to inform me if a
                    vessel subject to the orders of the Navy Department can, without detriment to
                    the public service, be directed to assist the marshal in preventing the
                    departure from New York, or that vicinity, of any unlawful expeditions in aid of
                    the Cuban insurgents, to which the marshal refers, as believed to be in course
                    of preparation.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Geo. M. Robeson</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of the Navy.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
